redwood gpu: waits that come to nothing are told; the statistics line is two lines (0231, diagnostics only).

From the code audit after all-21's freeze (2026-11-18): gpuWait() reports only a wait of a second or more that fails;
shorter ones, and ones whose time was over, fail in silence, and the five-second statistics are printed only with a
submission. A core standing still under a caller that asks again in short waits leaves no line. Now a failed wait of
10 ms or more, or 2000 failed ones of any length, gives one line every two seconds at most: how many, the submission
waited for, the patience, the program, what the core is done with and what was given last.
The statistics line was cut at about 256 characters in every log, so "waits", "over before they began", "IOSurfaces
taken" and the buffer totals were never seen: they are a line of their own.
Nothing changes what is waited for or how long. Not run on hardware yet.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
index b8539c4..ff2d479 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ extern uint32_t gpu_log;
 bool redwood_gpu_done(uint32_t fence);
 bool redwood_gpu_rejected(void);       /* bsd/dev/spes_gpu_backend.h: the last 0 from submit was a refusal */
 uint32_t redwood_gpu_last(void);
+uint32_t redwood_gpu_completed(void);  /* 0231: bsd/dev/spes_gpu_backend.h, the last submission the core says it is done with */
 void redwood_gpu_worked(uint64_t * microseconds, uint32_t * submissions, uint32_t by[7]);
 void redwood_gpu_report(const char * why);
 bool redwood_gpu_recover(void);
@@ -284,6 +285,31 @@ gpuWait(uint32_t fence, uint64_t milliseconds)
 		redwood_gpu_report("no answer");
 		gGPUReported = !redwood_gpu_recover();
 	}
+	{
+		/*
+		 * 0231: a wait shorter than a second that comes to nothing said nothing at all, and the
+		 * five-second line is only printed with a submission: a core standing still under a caller
+		 * that asks again and again in short waits would be silent (one reading of all-21's freeze,
+		 * with "CPU wakes" violations from the moment the picture stopped). Every two seconds at most.
+		 */
+		static uint32_t failed;
+		static uint64_t told;
+		uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time(), every;
+
+		failed++;
+		nanoseconds_to_absolutetime(2 * NSEC_PER_SEC, &every);
+		/* (a frame's end asks with no patience at all, once a frame: only waits that meant it, or very many, are told) */
+		if ((told == 0 || now - told >= every) && (milliseconds >= 10 || failed >= 2000)) {
+			char program[32];
+
+			proc_selfname(program, sizeof(program));
+			IOLog("RedwoodGPU: %u waits came to nothing since the last such line; this one: submission %u, %llu ms, by %s; "
+			    "the core is done with %u, the last given is %u%s\n", failed, fence, milliseconds, program,
+			    redwood_gpu_completed(), redwood_gpu_last(), gGPUReported ? " (reported as stopped)" : "");
+			failed = 0;
+			told = now;
+		}
+	}
 	return false;
 }
 
